    summary: 'RLHF samples responses from the current policy, scores them with a reward model or a verifier, and updates the policy to increase reward while a KL penalty keeps it close to a frozen reference (usually the SFT model). PPO is the classical optimizer, with a separate value model and clipped policy-ratio objective. Critic-free variants such as GRPO estimate advantages from a group of samples per prompt instead of a value model.',
