    summary: 'DPO reparameterizes the RLHF objective so the optimal policy can be trained with a classification-style loss on preference pairs. The policy and a frozen reference are scored on the chosen and rejected responses, and the loss pushes the log-ratio of the chosen up relative to the rejected. There is no reward model to train and no rollout loop, which makes it far simpler and cheaper than PPO, at the cost of being offline.',
